# Root .dockerignore — backend images build from the REPO ROOT context (so pnpm
# can resolve workspace:* deps). Keep that context lean: exclude installed deps,
# build output, VCS, secrets, and heavy unrelated trees. package.json files,
# pnpm-lock.yaml, and pnpm-workspace.yaml are intentionally NOT excluded — the
# pnpm install graph needs them.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/dist-*
# Cargo build output: a local build leaves gigabytes here, and every image builds its own.
/clis/target
/backend/target
.git
# The contract crates' recorded exchanges, the loaders of them and the examples the integration tests run are test inputs: no image builds them, so an edit to one must neither
# rebuild an image nor change its content hash (`wf` drops what this file excludes from the hash)
/libraries/agent-api/*/tests
/libraries/agent-api/*/examples
/libraries/agent-api/*/src/testing.rs
/libraries/agent-api/*/src/testing
# The agent service's replayed cassettes, its integration test and the Rust port's driver (an example of its service core) are read by tests only
/backend/remote-chat-agent/rs/tests/cassettes
/backend/remote-chat-agent/rs/tests/integration.rs
/backend/remote-chat-agent/service-core/examples
# The Orca crates' mimic drivers (examples) and the integration test that replays them are read by tests only
/clis/orca-serve/*/examples
/clis/orca-serve/tests/integration/mimic_x2.rs
/clis/orca-serve/tests/integration/mimic_x6.rs
/clis/orca-serve/cassettes

# The T3 server's imported cassettes are replayed by its tests only
/clis/t3-serve/cassettes
**/.expo
**/*.log

# Secrets never enter an image. The generated `.env` and all `.env.*` (incl.
# `.env.defaults`) are excluded — deploy injects env at runtime via compose, so
# the image never needs them.
**/.env
**/.env.*

# Credential-bearing files that are gitignored (so absent in CI) but WILL exist
# in a developer's working tree — `COPY . .` would otherwise bake them into a
# locally-built image. Matters more now that images may be pushed to a registry.
**/terraform.tfvars
**/*.tfstate
**/*.tfstate.*
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/.oci
# Any NESTED .npmrc — those are untracked, per-developer, and are where a
# registry auth token would live.
**/.npmrc
# ...but NOT the repo-root one, which is COMMITTED, holds no credential (only
# hoist patterns + strict-ssl), and IS REQUIRED by the build: this repo sets
# shamefully-hoist=true, so installing without it produces a different
# node_modules layout than the app expects. `.npmrc` unprefixed matches only the
# context root, so nested ones stay excluded. Excluding this file was a mistake
# introduced while hardening this list — it is a build input, not a secret.
!.npmrc

# Heavy trees no backend image needs. Every `COPY . .` layer is keyed on the whole context, so a
# change under any of these would otherwise invalidate the install and build layers of every image.
# NOT frontend/ or features/: pnpm-workspace.yaml's patchedDependencies target packages only those
# use, and `pnpm deploy` fails with ERR_PNPM_UNUSED_PATCH when they are missing.
references/
docs/
.agents/
.claude/
.codex/
.opencode/
.github/
.conventions-reports/
.screenshots/
.superpowers/
frontend/mobile-learning-app/.expo
**/.turbo
**/coverage
